1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,480
Lu Le told me

3
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,600
that the Bolo Culture project
is having some issues.

4
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,400
Relax.

5
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,120
You just joined not long ago,

6
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,040
and things with Lin Long didn't end well.

7
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,920
It's inevitable that the project
is moving slowly.

8
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,920
They approved my proposal.

9
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,280
If you lead it personally

10
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:10,120
and bring in Mr. Pi,
plus some foreign global partner

11
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:11,600
for show,

12
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:13,280
this project should be good to go.

13
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:22,640
Well done.

14
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,840
By the way, have you gotten confirmed yet?

15
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,360
-Still a few days to go.
-Sit.

16
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,040
Congratulations.
Your probation period is ending early.

17
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,640
Once the contract is signed,

18
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,200
you'll be promoted to SBA,

19
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,840
Senior Business Analyst.

20
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,360
Thank you, Ms. Sha.

21
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:53,920
So, will Ms. Lin still be my mentor?

22
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,960
Mentors are only for junior analysts
who just joined.

23
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,200
You no longer "qualify" for that.

24
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,680
You're on my team from now on.

25
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,440
I'll do my best not to let you down.

26
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,560
CONSULTING PROJECT TEAM CONFIGURATION

27
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:10,120
A typical Maxmise

28
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,920
consulting project team
has about five people.

29
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,760
One partner. Shows up once a week.

30
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:17,480
One project manager. Three consultants.

31
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,000
On-site every day.

32
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,600
For this Bolo Culture project,
I'll be the project manager.

33
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:24,000
Cindy and Du Wen
will be the two consultants,

34
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,600
plus one business analyst as team members.

35
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:28,600
But because
the client specifically requested it,

36
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:32,040
Xu Chi will join as an exception
for the SBA role.

37
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,880
Now let Xu Chi give everyone
an overview of the project.

38
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:35,880
Sure.

39
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:42,600
Xu Chi's killing it.

40
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:45,520
It's only been a few months,
and she's already an SBA.

41
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,400
She's the first among us, right?

42
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:49,520
Honestly, the one who should feel
most embarrassed is Lin Long.

43
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,400
She gave Xu Chi such a hard time before.

44
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,920
Now Xu Chi has started her own project.

45
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,320
She doesn't even report
to Lin Long anymore.

46
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,040
-Hello, Ms. Lin.
-Hello.

47
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,760
<i>I'm not giving up.</i>

48
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,120
Once this phase is over,

49
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:16,600
I'm taking back everything I've given up.

50
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:29,640
Pregnant women can't drink coffee.
Don't you know?

51
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,480
I knew something
would go wrong the moment I heard.

52
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:36,240
Can't you have held out a little longer?

53
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,800
You were doing
such a good job playing along

54
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,880
with your husband and Sha Sha.

55
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,080
You've gotten this far,

56
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:45,080
and now you're going to blow it all?

57
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,560
How can I hold out?

58
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,800
The Bolo Culture project
was mine from the start.

59
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,520
But Sha Sha didn't even ask me

60
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,320
before putting
Cindy and Xu Chi on the team.

61
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:56,160
Anyone but them.
Why does it have to be those two?

62
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,000
This project will take
another three or four months.

63
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:03,280
You can't just go on maternity leave
halfway through, can you?

64
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:07,280
Besides, Xu Chi is the one
who closed this deal.

65
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:10,360
And Cindy just finished
the Sato Pharmaceuticals project.

66
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:12,600
She's on break now and available.

67
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,440
If I were Sha Sha, I'd make the same call.

68
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,400
Whose side are you on?

69
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:21,320
Don't turn your fire on me.

70
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:25,200
I'm telling you this
because I actually care about you.

71
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:28,760
Xu Chi's really come into her own now.

72
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,920
All we can do is stay calm, right?

73
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,360
There are so many people in the company.
Don't let them enjoy the show.

74
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:35,640
Just focus on having your baby safely.

75
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,440
Six months later,
you'll be back in the game.

76
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,480
That's what you say to someone
going to the execution ground.

77
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:43,800
You have to hit rock bottom
before you can bounce back.

78
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:55,800
Congratulations.

79
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:00,560
It's nothing.

80
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:03,920
All thanks to your guidance.

81
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,400
<i>Lin, there's a new</i>
<i>infant insurance plan recently.</i>

82
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,640
<i>I think it'd be perfect for you.</i>
<i>Let me send it over.</i>

83
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,200
PENGCHENG WANLI CHILDREN'S
OVERSEAS FURTHER-STUDY ENDOWMENT PLAN

84
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:26,440
<i>I'm interested. Run the numbers for me.</i>

85
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,200
<i>If I start from birth and aim for college,</i>

86
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:30,200
<i>what's the premium?</i>

87
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,440
<i>If you start from birth,</i>

88
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:35,280
<i>I'd recommend a 15-year payment plan.</i>

89
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,840
<i>About 120,000 per installment.</i>

90
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,360
<i>Hundred and twenty thousand?</i>

91
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:50,360
TRANSFER TO JIANG YONGGE -500,000.00

92
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:53,120
It's been this long.

93
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:55,160
Why didn't you ever tell me?

94
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,360
I forgot, okay?

95
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:59,520
It's not a big deal.
Do you have to blow up like this?

96
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:01,000
That's 500,000, Jiang Zhiwen.

97
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,440
Are you out of your mind?

98
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,360
I'm about to give birth any day now.

99
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:05,640
We're about to have another money pit.

100
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,240
You didn't even discuss it with me

101
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,800
before lending that much money to someone?

102
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:13,280
Someone? They're my parents!

103
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,720
Stop making a scene.

104
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:16,480
The postnatal care center
is already paid for.

105
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,360
How much could diapers and formula
possibly cost?

106
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:19,520
The baby's not even born yet,

107
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,680
and you're already thinking
that far ahead?

108
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,080
Why don't you save up
for his bride-price too?

109
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,960
<i>Legal has finished the review.</i>

110
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,800
<i>We accept Maxmise's team and quote.</i>

111
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:36,280
<i>Ready to sign anytime.</i>

112
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,200
Done!

113
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:48,160
<i>Look at you all worried now.</i>

114
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,200
Where was that energy
when you went drinking with others?

115
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:51,360
Jiang Zhiwen!

116
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,840
Didn't we agree?

117
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,240
This is over and done with!

118
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,400
I threw that drink
in that scoundrel's face,

119
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,720
and you yelled at me
in front of your colleagues.

120
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:58,640
I will never get over that!

121
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,600
Yes. It's in that Bolo Culture file.

122
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,520
Xu Chi?

123
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,280
WANGJING SOHO

124
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:19,400
Richard?

125
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:22,880
What's wrong?

126
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:24,480
Are you drunk?

127
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,480
A little.

128
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,880
Hey,

129
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:32,640
you sent me a WeChat message earlier

130
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:34,840
and then recalled it, right?

131
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:36,000
MESSAGE RECALLED

132
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:38,520
COULD I ASK YOU FOR SOME ADVICE, RICHARD?

133
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:39,920
THAT'S THE SITUATION. I DON'T WANT
TO TAKE UP TOO MUCH OF YOUR TIME

134
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,520
Why didn't you send it again later?

135
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,440
I waited for you for a long time.

136
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:48,280
I…

137
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:50,520
Do you need a tissue?

138
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,680
Forget that for now.

139
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:56,320
I can't get a designated driver.
Can you drive?

140
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:58,600
-Yes.
-Can you take me home?

141
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,240
I…

142
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:08,680
The car's navigation system
has my home address saved.

143
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,120
Okay.

144
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,920
Where's your car?

145
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:15,840
-The first black one.
-Okay.

146
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:17,640
Steady yourself. I'll be right there.

147
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,560
Thanks.

148
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,440
Oh my God. This car is way too tall.

149
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,560
Easy there.

150
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,200
I'm fine.

151
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:47,240
Let me recite it for you. Three point
one four one five nine two six

152
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:48,640
-three two three eight four six two…
-Stop reciting.

153
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:51,320
Do it in the car. Stop it. Easy.

154
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:54,000
-Thanks. Thank you.
-Careful.

155
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,680
-Thanks.
-Head.

156
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:16,360
Richard.

157
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,000
Are you okay, Richard?

158
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:19,840
I'm fine, thanks.

159
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,520
You sure?

160
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:24,160
Yeah.

161
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:38,360
-Drop me off here.
-Alright, alright.

162
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,920
-Message me when you get home.
-Easy.

163
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,520
-I'll treat you to a meal sometime.
-Watch it.

164
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,480
You okay?

165
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:49,400
Which finger was it?

166
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,280
I just moved in.

167
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,800
Do you have a backup password?

168
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,720
I'm heading out now.

169
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,760
I'll close the door for you.

170
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,640
Are you okay?

171
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:31,640
Richard. Are you alright?

172
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,280
Don't sleep here.

173
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:40,160
You'll catch a cold.

174
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,200
Get up.

175
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:43,560
Easy there.

176
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:44,720
Easy.

177
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,120
Careful.

178
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,040
Easy there.

179
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:01,160
Wait!

180
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:03,800
Here, here. The bed.

181
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:33,880
TAKE A PICTURE AND SEARCH

182
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:38,080
2023 RAINER LIGHT RED
FROM RAINER SAUER ESTATE, 4,988 YUAN

183
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,240
-Glad that got sent.
-You're awake.

184
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,320
What are you doing here?

185
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:21,520
I… I didn't mean to stay.

186
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:24,840
<i>I got an urgent request</i>

187
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,720
<i>right as I was about to leave last night.</i>

188
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:29,040
<i>Xu Chi, I'm in London right now.</i>

189
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:31,440
<i>Once you get this email,</i>
<i>update the following data</i>

190
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:33,280
<i>in the low-altitude economy report</i>
<i>you compiled last time</i>

191
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:35,360
<i>and send it to me immediately.</i>
<i>I need it right away.</i>

192
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:44,120
<i>I figured I'd just reply</i>
<i>to the email here.</i>

193
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,360
Not sure how I fell asleep.

194
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:52,280
-Xu Chi?
-Richard?

195
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:53,520
Can you take me home?

196
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:10,960
I'm so sorry.

197
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:13,000
I blacked out last night.

198
00:17:14,079 --> 00:17:15,280
I put you through…

199
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:18,040
I'm not some naive little girl.

200
00:17:18,119 --> 00:17:19,960
It's just getting drunk.

201
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:21,920
I used to take my ex-boyfriend
back to his dorm.

202
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:27,000
Drunk people all act pretty much the same.

203
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:30,960
By the way,

204
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,960
there's a bottle of wine
broken in your bathroom.

205
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:40,080
You knocked it over yourself.
I cleaned it up for you.

206
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,560
2023 RAINER LIGHT RED
FROM RAINER SAUER ESTATE, 4,988 YUAN

207
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,560
No worries. Thanks.

208
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:56,200
What are you laughing at?

209
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:02,600
-Last night… You don't remember?
-What did I do last night?

210
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:06,760
"Which…? Which finger was it?

211
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:09,720
This one? This one?

212
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,200
I… I just moved in."

213
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:14,120
You okay?

214
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:18,360
Which finger was it?

215
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,800
<i>I just moved in.</i>

216
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:23,000
"I… I just moved in."

217
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:26,640
You want some water?

218
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:28,640
No thanks.

219
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:33,640
You seemed more like
a real person last night.

220
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:36,840
Usually, you look serious. Thanks.

221
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:39,760
So elite and high-end.

222
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:42,560
I once described you to Bu Tianna.

223
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:46,280
She said you're just a poser.

224
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,840
A few days ago, I was your idol.

225
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:51,040
Now I'm your joke.

226
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,560
So, learn from my mistake.

227
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,800
Even for work, don't drink that much.

228
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:57,520
Such a vibe…

229
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:00,360
Please don't use that word.
I'm more like your big brother at best.

230
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:04,280
Fine. Ye. Ye the Legend.

231
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:06,480
I have to go.

232
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:08,760
I have to be at work in two hours.

233
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:10,440
-Let me drive you.
-Don't bother.

234
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,520
I live really close.

235
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:15,400
Just turn the corner over there.
It's a white three-story building.

236
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,240
9 Days Inn?

237
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,040
Yeah.

238
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:23,160
The room
isn't even a tenth the size of yours,

239
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,400
but it's the same neighborhood.

240
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,120
So I've got the same good taste as you.

241
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,480
I need to hurry back
and wash my lucky outfit.

242
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:31,640
I finally landed my first deal.

243
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:32,800
Let me wash it for you!

244
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:35,680
I… I didn't mean anything by it.

245
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,000
It's a serviced apartment.
They have 24-hour room service.

246
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,280
They can have it done within an hour.

247
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,160
Red wine stains are hard to get out.

248
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,440
This is your first deal.
It's important to you, right?

249
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:47,280
It's fine. I can wash it myself.

250
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:48,640
We can have breakfast while we wait.

251
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:52,280
Just think of it as my thank-you
for driving me home last night.

252
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:55,680
Alright?

253
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,200
I've been in Beijing so long,

254
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,720
but I've never seen
a view like this before.

255
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:10,520
Isn't Maxmise's office building
taller than this?

256
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:12,360
It's different.

257
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:14,800
The view may be the same,

258
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:17,520
but the mood you bring to it isn't.

259
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:25,720
You live in a place this big
all by yourself.

260
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,920
It must be pretty expensive.

261
00:20:28,840 --> 00:20:31,920
I don't know. The car and the apartment
are both company rentals.

262
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,800
Once you make partner and get global pay,

263
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:38,880
Maxmise will offer you the same perk.

264
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:41,200
You know how our industry is.

265
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,760
You barely spend
a few days at home a month.

266
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,200
Home is just a place to store your stuff.

267
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:52,040
I appreciate the comfort

268
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,480
and encouragement.

269
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:57,480
Richard,

270
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:02,200
I landed this project with Bolo Culture.
But that's just the first step.

271
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:06,640
I will become who you are now.
I definitely will.

272
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:07,880
What am I like?

273
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,000
I'm not as great as you think.

274
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:14,160
All that glamor and sophistication

275
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:17,040
is just a facade
for getting by in this world.

276
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:20,120
You're right. A lot of people buy into it,

277
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,800
so it fools some people.

278
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:24,560
But behind the emperor's new clothes,

279
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,320
I'm just an ordinary person.

280
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,880
I boil water
and make instant noodles myself.

281
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:31,240
I have plenty of weak
and useless moments too.

282
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:32,840
Like yesterday.

283
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:35,840
I got wasted
because I had to entertain a client.

284
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,440
You're already a partner.

285
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:40,040
You still have to do
that kind of social drinking?

286
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,720
Of course.

287
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:46,480
Our whole lives
are about trading what we have

288
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:47,920
for what we want,

289
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,920
tirelessly, and unremittingly.

290
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:57,000
Outdated inspirational quotes. So cheesy.

291
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:01,360
Anyway, I'm going
to buy my mom's old apartment,

292
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:03,160
drink the same fine wine as you,

293
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:05,200
and become a partner just as great as you.

294
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:07,440
And I'll make every client fear me.

295
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:09,400
They won't dare question
a single word of my proposals.

296
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:12,040
Good. Then I'll be the first
to congratulate you.

297
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:37,040
Zhao Heng says I'm just lucky.

298
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:39,080
That I somehow pull through
at every critical moment,

299
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:41,000
and that's how I landed
the Bolo Culture project.

300
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:42,280
Don't be too modest.

301
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:45,440
Even a lucky break
requires strong foresight.

302
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:49,120
With Bolo Culture,
you at least grasped one key point.

303
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:50,480
Sometimes,

304
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:53,360
consulting isn't about plotting
grand blueprints for companies.

305
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:55,640
It's about getting paid
to be the client's mouthpiece.

306
00:22:56,840 --> 00:22:58,480
The client wants something
but doesn't want to say it,

307
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,760
so we propose it.

308
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:01,760
The client wants to do something
but doesn't want to take the blame,

309
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:03,160
so we push it forward.

310
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:04,240
If it works, everyone's happy.

311
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:06,280
If it fails, it's all on us.

312
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:08,160
And the client is always right.

313
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,080
When you put it that way,

314
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:12,480
I do seem pretty professional.

315
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,960
No wonder Sha Sha promoted me so quickly.

316
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:16,320
She must really see my potential.

317
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:19,040
Don't get cocky
just because I praised you.

318
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:25,120
-Bye.
-Bye.

319
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:30,920
Morning.

320
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:35,600
Same outfit.

321
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:39,440
I pulled an all-nighter
working last night.

322
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:44,240
He's that polished scumbag poser
you were talking about?

323
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:47,960
I ran into him while buying breakfast
and he gave me a ride.

324
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:50,200
Turns out his building
is right across the street,

325
00:23:50,280 --> 00:23:52,200
-and our parking garages--
-I didn't ask anything,

326
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:53,440
but you explained all that yourself.

327
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:55,920
Are you feeling guilty,
or are you feeling guilty?

328
00:23:59,400 --> 00:24:00,840
Why are you so interested in me today?

329
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:04,640
Don't tell me you're jealous
I got promoted to SBA before you?

330
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:10,040
Jealous of you?

331
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,120
There's a better chance

332
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:14,640
of Zhao Heng getting with me
than me being jealous of you.

333
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:17,400
Probably this week, Ande Energy

334
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:19,960
will come in and sign
the project cooperation agreement with me.

335
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:21,360
Not a huge deal.

336
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:23,040
Just twice the size of your project.

337
00:24:23,760 --> 00:24:25,520
Congratulations. Warmest congratulations.

338
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:27,440
Don't worry. I'll be super jealous of you.

339
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:36,680
Alright. Stop pretending you don't care.

340
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:39,360
Ande Energy's CEO
used to work under my dad.

341
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:40,920
Many say

342
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,640
even if he makes this project happen,
it's nothing but a favor-based deal.

343
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,480
Connections are part of the resources.

344
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:49,920
Why else would Maxmise bother
with the alumni network

345
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:51,920
and keep former employees happy?

346
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:55,040
Because former employees bring in
about half of our business.

347
00:24:55,760 --> 00:24:57,440
Sha Sha said even if Su Su quits,

348
00:24:57,520 --> 00:24:59,080
she'll get N+6 severance

349
00:24:59,160 --> 00:25:00,520
and a personal recommendation letter.

350
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:01,480
And

351
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,720
it's not like Ande Energy's money
belongs to the CEO personally.

352
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,360
If your proposal wasn't good enough,

353
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:07,200
would their internal
feasibility analysis pass?

354
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:09,040
Risk assessment? Legal compliance?

355
00:25:12,040 --> 00:25:12,880
You had better resources

356
00:25:12,960 --> 00:25:14,640
and a broader perspective
than me from day one.

357
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:17,160
But I'm not going to dwell
on what I can't change.

358
00:25:17,760 --> 00:25:19,240
After all, I've got things
I'm better at than you.

359
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:21,560
Like rapid analysis and luck.

360
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:24,800
So as long as we're strong enough,
our weaknesses won't become flaws.

361
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:28,720
No. Our flaws won't become weaknesses.

362
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,280
Who taught you that?

363
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:36,400
Sha Sha or that poser?

364
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:40,720
I figured that out myself
from all the times

365
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:42,040
I went up against Lin Long.

366
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:48,680
This one.

367
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:50,360
Yeah, thanks.

368
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:54,400
-Morning.
-I'm looking for our packages.

369
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:56,040
Hold on. Let me find them for you.

370
00:25:58,280 --> 00:25:59,480
Morning, Ms. Lin.

371
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:07,200
She's wearing
yesterday's outfit too, right?

372
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:11,800
Is something going on with her family?

373
00:26:19,040 --> 00:26:21,760
-Xu Chi, let's go.
-Coming.

374
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:45,920
<i>Don't be upset. We'll strike back later.</i>

375
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:52,800
You blocked me?

376
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:55,040
Why?

377
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,000
Anyone with a shred
of emotional intelligence

378
00:26:58,080 --> 00:26:59,240
wouldn't ask that question.

379
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:19,640
<i>How can I hold out?</i>

380
00:27:19,720 --> 00:27:22,000
<i>The Bolo Culture project</i>
<i>was mine from the start,</i>

381
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:23,560
<i>but Sha Sha didn't even ask me</i>

382
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:24,880
<i>before putting</i>
<i>Cindy and Xu Chi on the team.</i>

383
00:27:25,760 --> 00:27:28,320
<i>Anyone but them.</i>
<i>Why does it have to be those two?</i>

384
00:28:11,080 --> 00:28:12,240
<i>Dear,</i>

385
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:14,200
<i>what project is Richard Ye working on now?</i>

386
00:28:14,280 --> 00:28:15,120
LIN LONG, CELINE

387
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:16,240
<i>Tianhe Air.</i>

388
00:28:16,920 --> 00:28:19,520
<i>He's helping them transition from</i>
<i>a low-cost differentiated service model</i>

389
00:28:19,600 --> 00:28:21,040
<i>to a full-service strategy.</i>

390
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:24,520
<i>This kind of transition is gonna take</i>
<i>a ten-figure investment, right?</i>

391
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:28,720
<i>Otherwise, why would our boss</i>
<i>have directly poached him as a partner?</i>

392
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:42,160
<i>I heard he's been getting close</i>
<i>to some girl lately.</i>

393
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:44,560
<i>That gossip doesn't sound right.</i>

394
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:46,240
<i>Isn't his wife a lawyer?</i>

395
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:48,560
<i>Even if a girl wanted to steal him away,</i>

396
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:51,280
<i>she'd need the time and guts for it.</i>

397
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:01,120
<i>You want to blow things up, do you?</i>

398
00:29:01,200 --> 00:29:02,160
Let me make this clear.

399
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:05,240
Know what you should do
and what you shouldn't.

400
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:06,400
Got it.

401
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:09,320
Why did you speak
without my permission just now?

402
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:11,800
<i>You joined Maxmise just to replace me.</i>

403
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:27,320
<i>Yes, it's been signed.</i>

404
00:29:29,280 --> 00:29:32,680
Yes, yes. This is all
thanks to you, Richard.

405
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:36,760
Okay. Send the documents over
by courier then.

406
00:29:36,840 --> 00:29:38,320
I'll review them right away.

407
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:08,720
Let's have lunch, Zhao Heng.

408
00:30:09,280 --> 00:30:10,240
Okay.

409
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:14,880
Come on, Senior Business Analyst.

410
00:30:15,800 --> 00:30:16,800
Time to eat.

411
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:18,520
-Be right there.
-Alright.

412
00:30:58,800 --> 00:30:59,640
<i>Signee…</i>

413
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:00,560
FIRST COPY-CONFIDENTIAL DOCUMENT
ACKNOWLEDGMENT-OF-RECEIPT FORM

414
00:31:00,640 --> 00:31:01,640
<i>Ye Xinzhi?</i>

415
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:08,880
Sha Sha!

416
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:11,680
I want to report something.

417
00:31:12,320 --> 00:31:15,080
Xu Chi has seriously violated
company employee standards

418
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:16,200
and professional ethics.

419
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:18,680
The Bolo Culture project
wasn't secured by her alone.

420
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:21,080
It was all C&amp;C Consulting's partner,
Ye Xinzhi, helping her.

421
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:23,640
-Ye Xinzhi?
-Think about it.

422
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:25,040
How long has she been out of school?

423
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:27,080
How could she have landed
such a big deal on her own?

424
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:30,040
And Ye Xinzhi even gave her
his projects of C&amp;C Consulting to work on.

425
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:32,560
C&amp;C Consulting. That's our competitor.

426
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:33,920
Lin Long,

427
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:35,880
-those are serious accusations--
-I have proof, Sha Sha.

428
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:39,080
Xu Chi is very likely
a corporate spy sent by C&amp;C Consulting.

429
00:31:39,160 --> 00:31:40,920
She's here to steal our trade secrets.

430
00:31:41,600 --> 00:31:43,280
Step by step,
she's been trying to push me out

431
00:31:43,360 --> 00:31:44,840
and replace me.

432
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:46,920
This was all planned
from the very beginning.

433
00:31:53,360 --> 00:31:55,840
Ms. Lin, what are you talking about?
I don't understand at all.

434
00:31:56,760 --> 00:31:58,640
Still playing dumb even now?

435
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:00,960
Don't tell me you don't know Ye Xinzhi.

436
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:02,480
I do know him.

437
00:32:03,320 --> 00:32:04,360
But I met him

438
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:05,880
at the consulting industry summit
that you took me to.

439
00:32:06,520 --> 00:32:08,200
You even told me
to take the chance to network

440
00:32:08,280 --> 00:32:09,520
with more people in the industry.

441
00:32:09,600 --> 00:32:11,800
Mr. Pi is giving a speech
at the summit tomorrow afternoon.

442
00:32:11,880 --> 00:32:14,760
I'll bring you along.
You can meet some people in the circle.

443
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:16,760
Alright. Thanks, Ms. Lin.

444
00:32:16,840 --> 00:32:19,760
Hello, everyone. I'm Ye Xinzhi
from C&amp;C Consulting.

445
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:21,480
What are you talking about?

446
00:32:22,080 --> 00:32:24,480
I never introduced you two,
and I never said any of that.

447
00:32:24,560 --> 00:32:26,720
Why are you lying
through your teeth like this?

448
00:32:26,800 --> 00:32:28,240
Lin Long, calm down.

449
00:32:28,920 --> 00:32:30,040
Get to the point.

450
00:32:30,120 --> 00:32:31,520
You said you have proof

451
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:32,960
that Xu Chi worked
on Ye Xinzhi's C&amp;C Consulting projects.

452
00:32:33,040 --> 00:32:34,200
Can you show it?

453
00:32:38,200 --> 00:32:39,040
Here it is.

454
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:43,280
Ye Xinzhi just landed the Tianhe Air
digital transformation project.

455
00:32:43,360 --> 00:32:44,760
It's huge news in the industry.

456
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:47,520
But he handed Tianhe Air'
internal confidential documents

457
00:32:48,120 --> 00:32:49,000
over to Xu Chi.

458
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:58,160
Xu Chi, how do you explain this?

459
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:01,520
What proof do you have
that this came from Ye Xinzhi?

460
00:33:02,120 --> 00:33:02,960
Don't you remember?

461
00:33:04,200 --> 00:33:08,480
The confidentiality sign-off section
has Ye Xinzhi's signature on it.

462
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:13,240
Can I take a look? I don't remember
there being a signature on this.

463
00:33:18,120 --> 00:33:19,040
See for yourself.

464
00:33:25,280 --> 00:33:26,120
CASE FILE

465
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:27,640
There's nothing.

466
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:36,400
SIGNEE

467
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:38,600
RECEIVED BY

468
00:33:40,400 --> 00:33:41,320
This is impossible.

469
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:49,840
CONFIDENTIAL DOCUMENT
ACKNOWLEDGMENT-OF-RECEIPT FORM

470
00:33:56,760 --> 00:33:59,120
Ms. Sha, you know I always like
to collect industry information

471
00:33:59,200 --> 00:34:00,200
to practice my analytical skills.

472
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:02,240
This month, I chose the aviation industry.

473
00:34:02,920 --> 00:34:04,440
The information in this file
includes not only

474
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:07,160
Tianhe's publicly-available annual reports
over the years,

475
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:09,080
but also compiled analyses
from other think tanks.

476
00:34:09,159 --> 00:34:11,280
There are other airlines' data
in the back too.

477
00:34:11,360 --> 00:34:12,920
It's not internal documents at all.

478
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:15,520
And it has nothing to do
with confidentiality.

479
00:34:16,920 --> 00:34:17,760
I see.

480
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:21,120
This was all your plan.

481
00:34:22,679 --> 00:34:24,400
You set me up, didn't you?

482
00:34:27,480 --> 00:34:30,320
Ms. Lin, your condition
is really concerning.

483
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,040
Sha Sha, I have more evidence.

484
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:38,199
Look at these photos.

485
00:34:38,880 --> 00:34:40,000
That day…

486
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:44,480
I saw Ye Xinzhi
drop her off at work in the morning.

487
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:47,080
She's his mistress.
You can scroll further.

488
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:55,080
Lin Long.

489
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:57,680
Ye Xinzhi has been divorced
for a long time.

490
00:34:58,720 --> 00:35:01,640
He and I were in different class years
at Huaou Business School.

491
00:35:01,720 --> 00:35:04,200
He admitted it himself
at the last alumni gathering.

492
00:35:08,160 --> 00:35:09,200
But Xu Chi,

493
00:35:10,080 --> 00:35:12,240
while the company doesn't get involved
in employees' personal lives,

494
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,320
these photos…

495
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:16,080
A senior tripped.
I passed by and lent a hand.

496
00:35:16,160 --> 00:35:17,240
Am I really being framed for this?

497
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:18,200
We're all women here.

498
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:20,400
You should know how vicious
this kind of slander is.

499
00:35:22,560 --> 00:35:23,800
And

500
00:35:23,880 --> 00:35:25,280
if this photo
were taken from a wider angle,

501
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:27,400
you'd see Bu Tianna right there
in the elevator lobby.

502
00:35:28,040 --> 00:35:30,800
Am I really so brazen
that I'd carry on in front of a colleague?

503
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,720
Sha Sha, believe me. Don't listen to her.

504
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:38,960
All of this… It's all part of her plan.

505
00:35:39,640 --> 00:35:41,440
-She just wants to replace me!
-Enough!

506
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:45,680
I've held back
because you're pregnant and my senior.

507
00:35:46,280 --> 00:35:47,400
How much longer
am I supposed to take this?

508
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:51,160
This file was in my drawer.

509
00:35:51,240 --> 00:35:52,760
How did it end up with you?

510
00:35:55,720 --> 00:35:57,080
Isn't snooping through

511
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:59,880
someone else's drawer theft?
Doesn't reading someone else's files

512
00:35:59,960 --> 00:36:02,080
violate the company's
confidentiality policy? So,

513
00:36:03,120 --> 00:36:05,240
I'm requesting the surveillance footage
from our work area.

514
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:07,360
Let's get to the bottom of this.

515
00:36:25,080 --> 00:36:25,920
Xu Chi.

516
00:36:27,040 --> 00:36:28,680
Sometimes,

517
00:36:28,760 --> 00:36:31,560
young people can be too rigid.
I understand that.

518
00:36:31,640 --> 00:36:34,880
But this isn't as serious as you think.

519
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:37,200
-There's no need to escalate it to…
-I know.

520
00:36:38,560 --> 00:36:42,680
I'm a newbie,
so I should lie low and be tolerant.

521
00:36:42,760 --> 00:36:44,960
Especially since Ms. Lin is pregnant.

522
00:36:45,040 --> 00:36:47,760
For a long time before this,
I never told you

523
00:36:47,840 --> 00:36:49,000
what she did to me.

524
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:51,960
But please put yourself in my shoes.

525
00:36:52,040 --> 00:36:55,760
As my mentor, she never guided me
on the Bolo Culture project.

526
00:36:56,440 --> 00:36:57,880
Once we get to Bolo Culture,

527
00:36:57,960 --> 00:37:00,440
don't say a single word
without my permission.

528
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:02,120
-Got it?
-Got it.

529
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:03,480
As my supervisor,

530
00:37:04,080 --> 00:37:05,720
she tricked me
into drinking with an old man.

531
00:37:08,160 --> 00:37:09,800
Ms. Lin, I told you
I'm allergic to alcohol.

532
00:37:10,560 --> 00:37:12,120
So what do we do now?

533
00:37:13,440 --> 00:37:14,760
There you go. Right?

534
00:37:16,560 --> 00:37:17,920
As my colleague,

535
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:20,880
she slandered my reputation
and questioned my integrity.

536
00:37:20,960 --> 00:37:21,840
All of that…

537
00:37:23,800 --> 00:37:26,080
-isn't serious enough?
-Enough!

538
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:29,200
You're setting me up!

539
00:37:31,320 --> 00:37:32,160
I…

540
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:41,840
I know Ms. Lin is in a special situation,

541
00:37:41,920 --> 00:37:43,320
so this must be hard for you,

542
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:46,080
but let me make my position clear.

543
00:37:46,160 --> 00:37:49,000
Whatever you decide
to do about this, I'll accept it.

544
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:56,520
You're very good
at controlling your emotions.

545
00:37:57,560 --> 00:37:59,000
I take back what I said earlier.

546
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:00,720
You're more mature than I thought.

547
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:05,480
‎More mature…

548
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:12,360
-May I go back to work now?
-Go ahead.

549
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:14,200
Thanks.
